      "side": 1,
      "message": "Deleting the request from mAdvertiserRequests should go in pair with mSocketProvider.unrequestSocket; but the condition here isn\u0027t the same as the one in advertiserRequest.destroyAdvertiser: if forceDestroy\u003dtrue and mAdvertisers.size() \u003e 0, it would be removed from mAdvertiserRequests without calling unrequestSocket.\n\nHaving condition checks in 2 places that should be identical is error-prone, so I think it\u0027s best to keep the previous scheme that returned true when unrequestSocket has been called and the advertiser is to be deleted (if you implement the comment below \"return true if the interface advertiser has been destroyed\" would be always true).",
